{"id": "2026-10-10-news-us-sanctions-the-international-criminal-court", "date": "2026-10-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "US sanctions the International Criminal Court", "summary": "The United States put the International Criminal Court itself on its sanctions list on Friday 9 October, hours after a former ICC judge, Navi Pillay, won the Nobel Peace Prize", "url": "https://ofac.treasury.gov/recent-actions/20261009", "source_domain": "ofac.treasury.gov", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "The United States put the International Criminal Court itself on its sanctions list on Friday 9 October, hours after a former ICC judge, Navi Pillay, won the Nobel Peace Prize. The Treasury's Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC) added the court in The Hague to its list of blocked entities. It also issued four general licences, carve-outs that still allow some dealings with the court, including telecoms and enterprise software, pension payments and matters concerning ICC detainees. Washington had already sanctioned 13 of the court's judges and prosecutors, the ICC said. Le Monde reports that the measures only take full effect on Friday 9 April 2027, unless the court meets US demands first: cancel its arrest warrants for Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and former defence minister Yoav Gallant, close its investigation into alleged US and CIA abuses linked to Afghanistan, and amend its statute to bar prosecuting nationals of non-member states. Secretary of State Marco Rubio said that if allies did not \"rein in the court\" the US would dismantle it \"brick by brick\". The ICC called the sanctions \"an assault on the rule of law\". Canada, Denmark, Germany, France, Italy, Japan, the Netherlands and the UK said jointly that they \"strongly disagree\". Netanyahu thanked Washington. The US is not a party to the court's founding Rome Statute, which 125 states have ratified.", "why": "blocking the court as an institution reaches its bank accounts, IT suppliers and staff pay. That turns the US demands into a deadline for the European governments that host and fund the court.", "thread_id": "2026-10-10-news-us-sanctions-the-international-criminal-court", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-10", "event_date": "2026-10-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["International Criminal Court", "United States", "Marco Rubio", "Benjamin Netanyahu", "Navi Pillay"]}
{"id": "2026-10-10-news-trump-licenses-russian-diesel-imports", "date": "2026-10-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Trump licenses Russian diesel imports", "summary": "US President Donald Trump said on Friday 9 October that Vladimir Putin had agreed to release Russian diesel to US and world markets, and the Treasury issued a licence the same day allowing Russian diesel to be imported and sold", "url": "https://ofac.treasury.gov/recent-actions/20261009_33", "source_domain": "ofac.treasury.gov", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "US President Donald Trump said on Friday 9 October that Vladimir Putin had agreed to release Russian diesel to US and world markets, and the Treasury issued a licence the same day allowing Russian diesel to be imported and sold. According to Trump's post, Russia will supply more than 300,000 tonnes of diesel immediately, 500,000 tonnes in November and then 1 million tonnes. OFAC's General License 135 authorises the sale, delivery and import of Russian-origin diesel; DW reports that it runs until April 2027. A general licence is a blanket exemption from sanctions, here from the sweeping Russia sanctions law Trump signed last month. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky called the deal a \"gift to Putin\". Hours later a Ukrainian drone hit a Russian fuel site. The deal overshadowed the talks in Miami that Friday between US, Ukrainian and European officials. US envoy Steve Witkoff called them \"constructive\" and said they covered energy, grain exports, security guarantees and EU accession. Earlier that day, Putin had told Trump that a resumption of talks with Ukraine was unlikely.", "why": "the deal is aimed at US fuel prices ahead of the Tuesday 3 November midterms, but the licence eases pressure on Russia's war revenue while Washington's own envoys are trying to broker an end to the war.", "thread_id": "2026-10-10-news-trump-licenses-russian-diesel-imports", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-10", "event_date": "2026-10-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["United States", "Russia", "Ukraine", "Donald Trump", "Vladimir Putin"]}
{"id": "2026-10-10-news-china-agrees-to-curb-hybrid-car-exports-to-eu", "date": "2026-10-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "China agrees to curb hybrid car exports to EU", "summary": "EU trade commissioner Maroš Šefčovič said in Beijing on Friday 9 October that the EU and China had reached a \"shared understanding\" to moderate China's exports of hybrid and plug-in hybrid cars to the EU", "url": "https://ec.europa.eu/commission/presscorner/detail/en/statement_26_2124", "source_domain": "ec.europa.eu", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["economy", "geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "EU trade commissioner Maroš Šefčovič said in Beijing on Friday 9 October that the EU and China had reached a \"shared understanding\" to moderate China's exports of hybrid and plug-in hybrid cars to the EU. He said this \"opens the prospect of cutting China's exports by more than a half\". China also agreed to lower its standard import tariffs on almost €4 billion of EU exports, from car parts to olive oil and footwear, saving at least €225 million in duties, and to ease export licensing for rare earths and permanent magnets. Šefčovič called it \"only a first step\" and said EU leaders will take the final decision at the upcoming European Council. No implementing details were given.", "why": "it is the first concrete result of Brussels' push to rebalance a trade deficit it calls \"unsustainable\", and it targets hybrids, a segment the EU's tariffs on Chinese electric cars do not cover.", "thread_id": "2026-10-10-news-china-agrees-to-curb-hybrid-car-exports-to-eu", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-10", "event_date": "2026-10-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["European Union", "China", "Maroš Šefčovič"]}
{"id": "2026-10-10-news-magnitude-7-7-earthquake-strikes-panama", "date": "2026-10-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Magnitude-7.7 earthquake strikes Panama", "summary": "A magnitude-7.7 earthquake struck southern Panama shortly before 13:00 local time on Friday 9 October (19:56 Swiss time), followed by a magnitude-6.6 quake that afternoon and a 6.0 late that night", "url": "https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/eventpage/us6000u18k", "source_domain": "earthquake.usgs.gov", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A magnitude-7.7 earthquake struck southern Panama shortly before 13:00 local time on Friday 9 October (19:56 Swiss time), followed by a magnitude-6.6 quake that afternoon and a 6.0 late that night. The US Geological Survey placed the epicentre 12 km west-southwest of Pitaloza Arriba, at a shallow depth of about 10 km. Its automated impact model (PAGER) issued a red alert, its highest level. President José Raúl Mulino called it a \"major disaster\" that destroyed roads near the epicentre. RFI, however, reports only limited material damage and 27 people injured, after more than a hundred aftershocks. Local media reported that the historic Church of San Atanasio in Los Santos province collapsed. A tsunami warning for the Pacific coasts of Central and South America was lifted the same day, and the Panama Canal kept operating.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-10-news-magnitude-7-7-earthquake-strikes-panama", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-10", "event_date": "2026-10-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Panama", "USGS", "José Raúl Mulino"]}
{"id": "2026-10-10-news-delhi-sealed-off-before-election-chief-protest", "date": "2026-10-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Delhi sealed off before election-chief protest", "summary": "Indian authorities sealed off central New Delhi on Saturday 10 October ahead of a youth-led rally demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar, and police detained the leaders of the Cockroach Janta Party (CJP), the movement that called it", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/10/india-deploys-police-and-restricts-transport-ahead-of-mass-protest-in-delhi", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Indian authorities sealed off central New Delhi on Saturday 10 October ahead of a youth-led rally demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar, and police detained the leaders of the Cockroach Janta Party (CJP), the movement that called it. The protests target a revision of the voter rolls that has removed more than 130 million names. Critics say it favours Prime Minister Narendra Modi's BJP; the Election Commission says it removes duplicate and ineligible entries. According to ANI, authorities closed 57 metro stations from Friday night, cancelled long-distance trains and cut mobile internet within 4 km of the protest site. The CJP says at least 10,000 people have been detained across the country . India's Supreme Court said on Friday that some trains must still run.", "why": "the near-daily protests have turned a technical voter-roll clean-up into a sustained street challenge to the body that runs India's elections.", "thread_id": "2026-10-10-news-delhi-sealed-off-before-election-chief-protest", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-10", "event_date": "2026-10-10", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["India", "Cockroach Janta Party", "Election Commission of India", "Gyanesh Kumar"]}
{"id": "2026-10-10-news-lai-says-defence-build-up-aims-to-deter-war", "date": "2026-10-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Lai says defence build-up aims to deter war", "summary": "Taiwan's President Lai Ching-te said in his National Day address on Saturday 10 October that \"our aim by increasing investment in national defense is not to provoke; rather, it is to deter war.\" He accused China of using \"military and gray-zone activities\" (pressure that stops short of open war) to ", "url": "https://english.president.gov.tw/News/7226", "source_domain": "english.president.gov.tw", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Taiwan's President Lai Ching-te said in his National Day address on Saturday 10 October that \"our aim by increasing investment in national defense is not to provoke; rather, it is to deter war.\". He accused China of using \"military and gray-zone activities\" (pressure that stops short of open war) to change the status quo across the Taiwan Strait. He welcomed US–China dialogue but said it requires \"respect for the right of the people of Taiwan to exist\".", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-10-news-lai-says-defence-build-up-aims-to-deter-war", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-10", "event_date": "2026-10-10", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Taiwan", "Lai Ching-te", "China"]}
{"id": "2026-10-10-news-uae-says-flydubai-co-pilot-planned-9-11-style-cr", "date": "2026-10-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "UAE says Flydubai co-pilot planned 9/11-style crash", "summary": "UAE Attorney General Hamad Saif al-Shamsi said on Friday 9 October that the Omani co-pilot who attacked his captain with an axe on the Flydubai flight from Dubai to Tel Aviv had planned to crash the plane into Ben Gurion airport, in an attack he modelled on 11 September 2001", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/uae-omani-flydubai-co-pilot-planned-suicide-attack/a-79621960", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["security"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "UAE Attorney General Hamad Saif al-Shamsi said on Friday 9 October that the Omani co-pilot who attacked his captain with an axe on the Flydubai flight from Dubai to Tel Aviv had planned to crash the plane into Ben Gurion airport, in an attack he modelled on 11 September 2001. According to the statement carried by state media, the man flew the route twice beforehand to learn it, and his background checks on joining Flydubai in January 2026 showed no sign of extremist views. Passengers overpowered him on Wednesday 30 September, and the plane made an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-10-news-uae-says-flydubai-co-pilot-planned-9-11-style-cr", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-10", "event_date": "2026-10-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Flydubai", "United Arab Emirates", "Israel"]}
{"id": "2026-10-10-news-esther-friedli-rules-out-federal-council-bid", "date": "2026-10-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Esther Friedli rules out Federal Council bid", "summary": "St Gallen SVP senator Esther Friedli, seen as a front-runner to succeed Guy Parmelin on the Federal Council, said on Friday 9 October that she will not stand", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/bundesratswahl-esther-friedli-verzichtet", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "St Gallen SVP senator Esther Friedli, seen as a front-runner to succeed Guy Parmelin on the Federal Council, said on Friday 9 October that she will not stand. She told the portal Toggenburg 24 that she could not imagine leaving the Council of States after three and a half years. Her candidacy would also have given St Gallen a second Federal Council seat alongside Karin Keller-Sutter (FDP). SVP parliamentary group leader Thomas Aeschi told Radio SRF on Saturday 10 October that he would push for \"at least two people\" on the party's ticket. The group decides on Friday 20 November, and the Federal Assembly elects Parmelin's successor on Wednesday 9 December. Zurich cantonal minister Natalie Rickli is among the names now being mentioned.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-10-news-esther-friedli-rules-out-federal-council-bid", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-10", "event_date": "2026-10-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Esther Friedli", "SVP", "Federal Council", "Guy Parmelin", "Thomas Aeschi"]}
{"id": "2026-10-10-news-swiss-ukraine-reconstruction-accord-takes-effect", "date": "2026-10-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss–Ukraine reconstruction accord takes effect", "summary": "Switzerland's agreement with Ukraine on cooperation in its reconstruction entered into force on Friday 9 October, after the referendum deadline passed unused on Thursday 8 October", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/Ef89hHZk5zK-", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Switzerland's agreement with Ukraine on cooperation in its reconstruction entered into force on Friday 9 October, after the referendum deadline passed unused on Thursday 8 October. It lets Kyiv choose goods and services that the Confederation then buys from Swiss firms through public procurement and delivers as financial aid. It covers all Swiss companies, with energy and infrastructure named as priorities. The agreement was signed on Thursday 10 July 2025 and approved by both chambers in the 2026 summer session.", "why": "it is the legal basis for steering part of Switzerland's Ukraine programme for 2025–2028 to Swiss suppliers.", "thread_id": "2026-10-10-news-swiss-ukraine-reconstruction-accord-takes-effect", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-10", "event_date": "2026-10-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland", "Ukraine", "Federal Council"]}
{"id": "2026-10-10-news-edmond-de-rothschild-faces-french-laundering-tri", "date": "2026-10-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Edmond de Rothschild faces French laundering trial", "summary": "Geneva bank Edmond de Rothschild will stand trial at the end of October before the criminal court in Marseille for organised money laundering, Le Temps reported on Friday 9 October", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/exclusif-la-banque-edmond-de-rothschild-va-comparaitre-en-france-pour-blanchiment-en-bande-organisee", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Geneva bank Edmond de Rothschild will stand trial at the end of October before the criminal court in Marseille for organised money laundering, Le Temps reported on Friday 9 October. The case concerns a former deputy head of its wealth-management service, accused of moving CHF 6.7 million in December 2009 to an offshore account at the group's Nassau subsidiary. A San Marino bank and seven other defendants will also be tried. At the time, laundering the proceeds of tax fraud was not yet a crime in Switzerland.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-10-news-edmond-de-rothschild-faces-french-laundering-tri", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-10", "event_date": "2026-10-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Edmond de Rothschild", "France", "Marseille"]}
